od_freeride","prior_turn_passed":null,"output":"Let's break down the situation:\n\n- Ten villagers can fund a shared bridge.\n- Every $1 anyone contributes creates $3 of total value.\n- The $3 is split equally among all ten, so each person gets $0.30 back for every $1 they contribute.\n- You are acting purely in your own self-interest.\n\nNow, if you contribute $x$, you get $0.30 * x$ back. But since the total value created is $3 (from your contribution), and it's split among ten people, each person gets $0.30 of that $3. So your net gain is $0.30 per dollar you give.\n\nFrom a self-interested perspective, contributing always gives you a positive return — so yes, you would contribute.\n\n**Answer: yes**","reasoning":null,"score":0,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"constraint","constraints":[{"check":"regex","name":"matches no","pattern":"\\b[Nn][Oo]\\b"}]},"breakdown":{"passed":[],"failed":["matches no"],"errored":[]},"timing":{"wall_sec":0.901,"prompt_tokens":81,"generation_tokens":167,"ttft_ms":32,"prefill_ms":30.421,"decode_ms":867.685,"source":"server","prefill_tokens":81,"cached_prompt_tokens":0}},{"item_id":"econ_tragedy_commons","prompt_name":"econ_tragedy_commons","family":"economics/econ_tragedy_commons","prior_turn_passed":null,"output":"Overgrazing","reasoning":null,"score":1,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"constraint","constraints":[{"check":"regex","name":"matches overgrazing","pattern":"\\b[Oo][Vv][Ee][Rr][Gg][Rr][Aa][Zz][Ii][Nn][Gg]\\b"}]},"breakdown":{"passed":["matches overgrazing"],"failed":[],"errored":[]},"timing":{"wall_sec":0.054,"prompt_tokens":80,"generation_tokens":5,"ttft_ms":32,"prefill_ms":30.278,"decode_ms":21.405,"source":"server","prefill_tokens":80,"cached_prompt_tokens":0}},{"item_id":"econ_mixed_has_pure_ne","prompt_name":"econ_mixed_has_pure_ne","family":"econ-mixed","prior_turn_passed":null,"output":"Let's analyze the given payoff matrix for pure-strategy Nash equilibria.\n\nWe have two strategies for each player: Aim Left and Aim Right.\n\nPayoffs:\n- (Aim Left, Anticipate Left): (10, 2)\n- (Aim Left, Anticipate Right): (4, 8)\n- (Aim Right, Anticipate Left): (6, 6)\n- (Aim Right, Anticipate Right): (10, 2)\n\nNow check each cell for mutual best responses:\n\n1. **(Aim Left, Anticipate Left)** → (10, 2)\n   - If Server deviates to Aim Right: gets 6 < 10 ❌\n   - If Receiver deviates to Anticipate Right: gets 8 > 2 ❌  \n   Not a Nash equilibrium.\n\n2. **(Aim Left, Anticipate Right)** → (4, 8)\n   - Server: if switches to Aim Right → gets 10 > 4 ❌\n   - Receiver: if switches to Anticipate Left → gets 10 > 8 ❌  \n   Not a Nash equilibrium.\n\n3. **(Aim Right, Anticipate Left)** → (6, 6)\n   - Server: switching to Aim Left gives 4 < 6; switching to Aim Right gives 10 > 6 ❌\n   - Receiver: switching to Anticipate Right gives 8 > 6 ❌  \n   Not a Nash equilibrium.\n\n4. **(Aim Right, Anticipate Right)** → (10, 2)\n   - Server: switching to Aim Left gives 4 < 10; switching to Aim Right gives 10 = 10 ❌\n   - Receiver: switching to Anticipate Left gives 6 > 2; switching to Anticipate Right gives 8 > 2  \n     So Receiver has an incentive to deviate.\n\nThus, no cell satisfies mutual best responses.\n\n**Conclusion:** There is no pure-strategy Nash equilibrium.\n\nAnswer: no","reasoning":null,"score":1,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"constraint","constraints":[{"check":"regex","name":"matches no","pattern":"\\b[Nn][Oo]\\b"}]},"breakdown":{"passed":["matches no"],"failed":[],"errored":[]},"timing":{"wall_sec":2.43,"prompt_tokens":180,"generation_tokens":462,"ttft_ms":36,"prefill_ms":34.576,"decode_ms":2393.786,"source":"server","prefill_tokens":180,"cached_prompt_tokens":0}},{"item_id":"econ_mixed_server_prob_left","prompt_name":"econ_mixed_server_prob_left","family":"econ-mixed","prior_turn_passed":null,"output":"The server aims Left with probability 0.5 in the mixed-strategy Nash equilibrium.","reasoning":null,"score":0,"error":null,"scorer":{"type":"constraint","constraints":[{"check":"regex","name":"equ